- op: discuss  # 1ffc
  at: '2026-02-18T13:44:37Z'  # 1ffc
  by: agent  # 1ffc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1ffc
  clock: 5  # 1ffc
  nonce: 1ffc  # 1ffc
  message: "D language cross-file resolution: The current analyzer resolves calls within a single file. For cross-file, need to handle D module imports (import std.algorithm) and track exported symbols per module to build accurate call edges across files."  # 1ffc
- op: discuss  # 8a46
  at: '2026-02-18T14:01:12Z'  # 8a46
  by: agent  # 8a46
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8a46
  clock: 6  # 8a46
  nonce: 8a46  # 8a46
  message: "D module system: Each file defines a module based on its path (std/algorithm.d -> std.algorithm). Public symbols are exported by default unless marked private. The cross-file resolver needs to build a module-to-symbol map from the filesystem layout."  # 8a46
- op: discuss  # 85a8
  at: '2026-02-18T14:41:45Z'  # 85a8
  by: agent  # 85a8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 85a8
  clock: 7  # 85a8
  nonce: 85a8  # 85a8
  message: "D also supports selective imports (import std.algorithm : sort) and renamed imports (import io = std.stdio). The cross-file resolver needs to track both the module path and the specific imported symbols."  # 85a8
- op: discuss  # 99c6
  at: '2026-02-18T14:55:14Z'  # 99c6
  by: agent  # 99c6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 99c6
  clock: 8  # 99c6
  nonce: 99c6  # 99c6
  message: "D mixin templates are another challenge for cross-file resolution. A mixin can inject code from one module into another at compile time, creating implicit dependencies that are not visible in import statements."  # 99c6
